  "question": {
    "text": "The hydrocarbon $(X)$ with molar mass $80 \\mathrm{~g} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$ and $90 \\%$ carbon has $\\ldots\\ldots$ degree of unsaturation.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/gyKrzfQ6ZImLhZhL3faiguGnbOSDIu-i6NZ7GClxRq0.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n\n$\\therefore$ Empirical formula is $\\mathrm{C}_3 \\mathrm{H}_4$\nMolecular mass $=80 \\mathrm{~g} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$.\nMolecular formula $=\\left(\\mathrm{C}_3 \\mathrm{H}_4\\right)_{\\mathrm{n}}$\n$\\mathrm{n}=\\frac{\\text { Molecular mass }}{\\mathrm{EF} \\text { mass }}=\\frac{80}{40}=2$\n$\\therefore$ Molecular formula is $\\mathrm{C}_6 \\mathrm{H}_8$\nDegree of unsaturation $=\\frac{2 \\times 6+2-8}{2}=3$",
    "image": null
  },
